        "instructions": [
          {
            "id": 206832,
            "primary_message": "Cut the tofu in half along the long side. Sandwich the tofu between clean towels or paper towels and place side by side on a baking sheet. Place a cutting board with something heavy on top and set aside to press out excess water.",
            "secondary_message": "2 (12 oz) pkg extra firm tofu"
          },
          {
            "id": 206833,
            "primary_message": "Using a strainer or colander, rinse the rice under cold, running water, then drain and transfer to a small saucepan. Add water and bring the mixture to a boil over high heat.",
            "secondary_message": "1 cup jasmine rice\n2 cup water"
          },
          {
            "id": 206834,
            "primary_message": "Peel and mince the garlic. In a medium bowl, combine garlic, sesame oil, soy sauce, and maple syrup to make a marinade for the tofu. ",
            "secondary_message": "2 cloves garlic\n2 tbsp toasted sesame oil\n¼ cup soy sauce\n2 tbsp pure maple syrup"
          },
          {
            "id": 206835,
            "primary_message": "Once the liquid with the rice comes to a boil, stir the mixture, cover the saucepan, and reduce the heat to low. Cook the rice until the liquid is fully absorbed, 15-18 minutes. Once done, remove the rice from the heat and let it stand, still covered, for 5 minutes.",
            "secondary_message": null
          },
          {
            "id": 206836,
            "primary_message": "Meanwhile, cut the tofu planks in half and then cut each half into 4 triangles. Place tofu in the bowl with the marinade and gently toss until well coated. Set aside. ",
            "secondary_message": null
          },
          {
            "id": 206837,
            "primary_message": "Wash and dry kale. Fold leaves in half lengthwise and slice off the stems. Chop or tear leaves into bite-sized pieces and transfer to a salad bowl. ",
            "secondary_message": "2 bunches kale"
          },
          {
            "id": 206838,
            "primary_message": "Wash, trim, and peel the carrots; coarsely grate and set aside.",
            "secondary_message": "2 medium carrots"
          },
          {
            "id": 206839,
            "primary_message": "Preheat a skillet over medium-high heat.",
            "secondary_message": null
          },
          {
            "id": 206840,
            "primary_message": "Wash, peel, and mince or grate the ginger. ",
            "secondary_message": "2 (1 inch) pieces ginger root"
          },
          {
            "id": 206841,
            "primary_message": "Once the skillet is hot, add oil and swirl to coat the bottom. Add the tofu and the marinade.  Cook until golden brown, 2-3 minutes per side. ",
            "secondary_message": "2 tbsp toasted sesame oil"
          },
          {
            "id": 206842,
            "primary_message": "Meanwhile, prepare the peanut sauce by whisking together ginger, peanut butter, chili-garlic sauce, soy sauce, maple syrup, and hot water in a small bowl. ",
            "secondary_message": "¼ cup natural peanut butter\n1 tbsp chili-garlic sauce\n2 tsp soy sauce\n2 tsp pure maple syrup\n3 tbsp water"
          },
          {
            "id": 206843,
            "primary_message": "Once the tofu is cooked, transfer to a plate, returning the skillet to the heat. Add kale and water to the skillet and cover with a lid. Allow to steam for 1 minute covered then uncover, stirring occasionally, for 1 minute more. ",
            "secondary_message": "½ cup water"
          },
          {
            "id": 206844,
            "primary_message": "Uncover the rice, fluff with a fork, and add sesame oil. Fold the oil into the rice. ",
            "secondary_message": "1 tbsp toasted sesame oil"
          },
          {
            "id": 206845,
            "primary_message": "To serve, divide rice between bowls, top with tofu, grated carrot, and kale; drizzle with peanut sauce and sprinkle with sesame seeds. Enjoy! ",
            "secondary_message": "2 tbsp sesame seeds"
          }
        ],
